    "manual_derivation": [
      "A captured class contributes only its class object identity as closure content; its member functions are added to a traversal worklist via vars(class).values().",
      "The traversal emits rows keyed by function identity/code/default/kwdefault/closure/cells and sorts the final rows. It records neither member name nor descriptor kind or name-to-function edge.",
      "Swap C.count_query and C.select_query while retaining both function objects. The class object identity and function set/rows remain unchanged, even though attribute lookup bindings differ.",
      "The predecessor separately recorded sorted(name,id(function),...) tuples for a captured class. Those named tuples change under the swap.",
      "Frozen worker actually creates local Facade with these two methods and captures it in graph_body/search lambda. It is not a module-owned class whose mapping is independently covered by the module callable_seal."
    ],
